From 71c5458e45593ecade8a2f5c48667559b27747cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Mon, 15 Jun 2026 08:58:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 36/42] tests/e2e: Playwright multi-tenant specs (login picker,
 switcher, onboarding)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Drives the patch-0033 UI in a real browser against a running
bifrost-http with BIFROST_MULTI_TENANT_ENABLED=true.

multi-tenant.spec.ts — three describe blocks:

  - "login picker": dropdown lists seeded tenants, login persists
    selection to localStorage, the public /api/session/tenants
    endpoint returns only {id, name, status} (guards against the
    auth-bypass whitelist accidentally leaking admin metadata).

  - "in-workspace switcher": TenantBadge reflects login choice,
    switching tenants updates badge + localStorage, hard reload
    preserves the selection.

  - "config isolation": tenant A's seeded provider is visible on
    A's providers page, not on B's. Today this passes via the
    patch-0034 baseQuery rewriter; if Stage 2 ever silently
    regressed, this is the spec that catches it.

onboarding.spec.ts — one continuous browser flow that exercises
the full new-tenant happy path the user asked for: login as admin,
pick "+ New tenant…" sentinel, supply a unique id → tenant
created on submit. Then /workspace/providers → add custom
openai-shaped provider pointed at the in-cluster vLLM Service
(http://bm-llms-qwen3-coder.llm-system.svc.cluster.local:8000),
add a provider key with explicit models, /workspace/virtual-keys
→ create a VK referencing the provider with an allowed-model
list. Validates every patch-0034 fix in one trip (key Models field
preservation, full schemas.Key payload round-trip, rich response
shapes so the optimistic cache updates don't crash with React
error boundaries).

pages/multi-tenant.page.ts — MultiTenantPage object encapsulating
gotoLogin / login / switchTenantTo / getPersistedTenantID. Uses
data-testid hooks ("tenant-badge", "tenant-option-new",
"new-tenant-id", "new-tenant-name") rather than label text so the
strings can be localized without breaking specs.

Wires require BIFROST_E2E_ADMIN_PASS for the login flow; specs
auto-skip when unset so the suite stays green on auth-disabled
dev servers.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
